WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.117 --> 00:00:20.622
Mr. Gwarg stared at his watch as he waited for the monsters to calm down.

2
00:00:20.623 --> 00:00:24.083
"We're losing precious time," he said.

3
00:00:24.084 --> 00:00:29.958
When everyone had finally grown quiet again, Mr. Gwarg grabbed his clipboard.

4
00:00:29.959 --> 00:00:33.877
"Let's review our Field Day rules."

5
00:00:33.878 --> 00:00:36.434
"Ugh." Mog groaned.

6
00:00:36.435 --> 00:00:39.495
"We've heard these rules twenty times already!

7
00:00:39.496 --> 00:00:41.852
Can't we just get started?"

8
00:00:41.853 --> 00:00:45.494
"That's enough, Mog!" Mr. Freaky snapped.

9
00:00:45.495 --> 00:00:47.304
"The rules are important.

10
00:00:47.305 --> 00:00:51.079
That's how everything stays under control around here."

11
00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:56.603
He took out his handkerchief and blew his noses.

12
00:00:56.604 --> 00:01:02.822
"Okay, first rule—no magic spells," Mr. Gwarg announced.

13
00:01:02.823 --> 00:01:07.796
"Aww!" Several witches and wizards started complaining.

14
00:01:07.797 --> 00:01:12.147
"What about hexes?" somebody asked. "Can we use those?"

15
00:01:12.148 --> 00:01:17.473
"No!" Mr. Gwarg snapped. "No magic whatsoever!"

16
00:01:17.474 --> 00:01:19.733
A vampire raised her hand.

17
00:01:19.734 --> 00:01:26.827
"Can I turn into a bat and fly around?"

18
00:01:26.828 --> 00:01:28.977
Mr. Gwarg blinked at her.

19
00:01:28.978 --> 00:01:32.868
"You're not even on a team, Vanessa," he said.

20
00:01:32.869 --> 00:01:37.332
"But if you were on a team, yes, you could do that.

21
00:01:37.333 --> 00:01:40.392
That's not magic—it's an ability."

22
00:01:40.393 --> 00:01:48.625
"So it's okay if I make my feet bigger to run faster?" Carly asked.

23
00:01:48.626 --> 00:01:51.240
The gym teacher scratched his head.

24
00:01:51.241 --> 00:01:56.100
"I guess so. But I don't think it would actually improve your speed."

25
00:01:56.101 --> 00:02:00.135
Monsters kept raising their hands to ask more questions.

26
00:02:00.136 --> 00:02:05.286
Finally Mr. Gwarg lifted his whistle and gave a long, loud blast.

27
00:02:05.287 --> 00:02:10.645
"I don't have time to answer all these questions.

28
00:02:10.646 --> 00:02:13.472
Look, there's really only one rule.

29
00:02:13.473 --> 00:02:17.540
And that's this one—just play fair.

30
00:02:17.541 --> 00:02:22.724
Now Team Orange and Team Black, line up for our first event.

31
00:02:22.725 --> 00:02:25.730
It's the tug-of-war!"

32
00:02:25.731 --> 00:02:31.414
"Phew," Ben murmured to Pixel. "That took forever."

33
00:02:31.415 --> 00:02:39.216
The spectators cheered as the two teams took their places in the center of the field.

34
00:02:39.217 --> 00:02:45.492
Ben could see that a long rope had been laid over a shallow pit filled with mud.

35
00:02:45.493 --> 00:02:50.312
The teams lined up on opposite sides of the pit.

36
00:02:50.313 --> 00:02:53.724
Then each player gripped the rope.

37
00:02:53.725 --> 00:02:58.368
Suddenly Ben spotted the sixth member of Team Orange.

38
00:02:58.369 --> 00:03:01.884
"Oh, no!" he gasped.

39
00:03:01.885 --> 00:03:06.109
Last in line on the opposite side of the rope was Gaby.

40
00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:09.633
And Gaby was strong—really strong!

41
00:03:09.634 --> 00:03:13.592
She must be what Zork meant by his "secret weapon."

42
00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:18.077
Waldo had spotted her too. "Not good," he muttered.

43
00:03:18.078 --> 00:03:21.150
"Gaby is even stronger when she's mad."

44
00:03:21.151 --> 00:03:25.895
Ben gulped. "And is she mad about something right now?"

45
00:03:25.896 --> 00:03:29.897
Waldo nodded. "She's really mad at me.

46
00:03:29.898 --> 00:03:33.992
She said that I should have made Mog choose her for Team Black."

47
00:03:33.993 --> 00:03:37.489
Ben drew in a breath.

48
00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:41.082
"Well, there's no time to worry about that now," he said.

49
00:03:41.083 --> 00:03:43.233
"We're about to start."

50
00:03:43.234 --> 00:03:49.443
"Okay, guys." Mog turned around to talk to his team from his spot as first in line.

51
00:03:49.444 --> 00:03:55.725
"Here's the plan. As soon as the game starts, pull the rope as fast and as hard as you can.

52
00:03:55.726 --> 00:03:58.567
Maybe we can take Team Orange by surprise."

53
00:03:58.568 --> 00:04:02.912
"Got it!" everybody said, gripping the rope tightly.

54
00:04:02.913 --> 00:04:05.426
Mr. Gwarg lifted his whistle.

55
00:04:05.546 --> 00:04:10.715
"The first team to pull the other team into the mud wins," he announced.

56
00:04:10.716 --> 00:04:12.844
"Is everybody ready?"

57
00:04:12.845 --> 00:04:18.448
Both team captains nodded, and then—tweet! The whistle blew to start the game.

58
00:04:18.449 --> 00:04:22.487
"Pull, Black!" Mog shouted. "Pull hard!"

59
00:04:22.488 --> 00:04:26.529
Ben and the others tugged as fast and as hard as they could.

60
00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:30.264
To Ben's surprise, Mog's plan worked perfectly.

61
00:04:30.265 --> 00:04:37.586
In an instant Zork and his team were flying across the ground, and Zork was teetering on the edge of the mud pit.

62
00:04:37.587 --> 00:04:48.138
"Pull!" Mog screamed. "Harder!"

63
00:04:48.139 --> 00:04:53.553
"Yes!" Ben thought. "Zork's going to fall in! We're going to win!"

64
00:04:53.554 --> 00:04:57.758
Then, with a loud ka-snap!, the rope broke.

65
00:04:57.759 --> 00:05:02.484
Both teams tumbled backward, landing hard on the ground.

66
00:05:02.485 --> 00:05:08.647
"Time out!" Mr. Gwarg rushed forward to look at the broken rope.

67
00:05:08.648 --> 00:05:12.930
"What in the world happened? I buy the best ropes in Monsterville.

68
00:05:12.931 --> 00:05:15.910
I've never seen one break before."

69
00:05:15.911 --> 00:05:19.310
Waldo went to take a look.

70
00:05:19.311 --> 00:05:22.855
"I can fix that, Mr. Gwarg. I know a good spell."

71
00:05:22.856 --> 00:05:25.754
"Me too!" Brunhilda called.

72
00:05:25.755 --> 00:05:29.871
"Monsters!" Mr. Freaky was flapping his arms.

73
00:05:29.872 --> 00:05:35.027
"What did Mr. Gwarg tell you—no magic during Field Day events!"

74
00:05:35.028 --> 00:05:37.373
"Sorry!" Waldo called.

75
00:05:37.374 --> 00:05:40.309
"We forgot," Brunhilda added.

76
00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:44.985
Mr. Gwarg ran to an equipment shed to get another rope.

77
00:05:44.986 --> 00:05:48.551
Then he told the two teams to line up again.

78
00:05:48.552 --> 00:05:51.663
"Okay, everyone, take your places."

79
00:05:51.664 --> 00:05:56.978
The teams gathered on their sides of the pit once more.

80
00:05:56.979 --> 00:06:02.943
"Go!" Mr. Gwarg shouted, and both teams began pulling with all their might again.

81
00:06:02.944 --> 00:06:10.105
This time, though, Team Orange wasn't surprised by Team Black's strategy; they were ready for it.

82
00:06:10.106 --> 00:06:17.534
Back and forth the rope tugged for several minutes, with neither team making much progress.

83
00:06:17.535 --> 00:06:24.583
The spectators on the field were cheering loudly as the cheerleaders did cartwheels across the field.

84
00:06:24.584 --> 00:06:28.252
"Go, Orange! Go, Black!"

85
00:06:28.253 --> 00:06:34.417
Then all at once, the air went deadly silent.
